{
 "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
 "rate": "+11%",
 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "He was halfway through the last box of peaches when the store went quiet.",
   "start": 0.05,
   "end": 3.4121621
  },
  {
   "text": "Not silent.",
   "start": 3.4121621,
   "end": 4.4369368
  },
  {
   "text": "Quiet.",
   "start": 4.4369368,
   "end": 5.18018
  },
  {
   "text": "The refrigerator hum, the radio low behind the register, the rain ticking on the skylights.",
   "start": 5.1801801,
   "end": 11.0923421
  },
  {
   "text": "Nineteen years old, alone on the closing shift, and a rent payment he couldn't make.",
   "start": 11.0923421,
   "end": 15.5968465
  },
  {
   "text": "He finished the row, taped the carton shut, and walked across the store to restock the other side.",
   "start": 15.5968466,
   "end": 20.7770267
  },
  {
   "text": "The automatic glass doors were on his way.",
   "start": 20.7770267,
   "end": 22.9279275
  },
  {
   "text": "Through them, the parking lot was a black mirror.",
   "start": 22.9279276,
   "end": 25.664414
  },
  {
   "text": "And something in it was moving.",
   "start": 25.664414,
   "end": 27.6238734
  },
  {
   "text": "A man, or what used to be a man, in a green coat, limping.",
   "start": 27.6238735,
   "end": 31.4639635
  },
  {
   "text": "He was pressed against a parked car, slamming one hand into the window.",
   "start": 31.4639635,
   "end": 35.4729724
  },
  {
   "text": "Again.",
   "start": 35.4729725,
   "end": 36.2387382
  },
  {
   "text": "And again.",
   "start": 36.2387382,
   "end": 37.049549
  },
  {
   "text": "The same motion every time, like a machine that had forgotten how to stop.",
   "start": 37.049549,
   "end": 41.0472966
  },
  {
   "text": "The stocker set down the box.",
   "start": 41.0472967,
   "end": 42.7590083
  },
  {
   "text": "He walked to the glass.",
   "start": 42.7590084,
   "end": 44.0653146
  },
  {
   "text": "Up close, the details were worse.",
   "start": 44.0653147,
   "end": 46.3851344
  },
  {
   "text": "Skin the colour of old leaves.",
   "start": 46.3851345,
   "end": 48.434684
  },
  {
   "text": "A jaw hanging wrong.",
   "start": 48.434684,
   "end": 49.729729
  },
  {
   "text": "Eyes that didn't look at anything.",
   "start": 49.729729,
   "end": 51.3400893
  },
  {
   "text": "Rain running off him in sheets, and he didn't seem to feel it.",
   "start": 51.3400894,
   "end": 54.5045037
  },
  {
   "text": "The thing turned.",
   "start": 54.5045038,
   "end": 55.6306299
  },
  {
   "text": "He ran for the shutter controls beside the door and hit the button.",
   "start": 55.6306299,
   "end": 58.8851343
  },
  {
   "text": "The steel shutter came down with a scream of metal, slow, too slow, grinding toward the floor while the thing outside turned toward the sound.",
   "start": 58.8851343,
   "end": 66.9932423
  },
  {
   "text": "Six seconds.",
   "start": 66.9932423,
   "end": 68.1756747
  },
  {
   "text": "That's how long it takes a steel shutter to seal a supermarket.",
   "start": 68.1756747,
   "end": 71.4189179
  },
  {
   "text": "He counted every one of them.",
   "start": 71.4189179,
   "end": 72.9954944
  },
  {
   "text": "When it finally hit the floor, the parking lot went dark and the store stayed bright.",
   "start": 72.9954945,
   "end": 77.2747737
  },
  {
   "text": "For the first time that night, he was safe.",
   "start": 77.2747737,
   "end": 79.3918907
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the thing outside looked up at the camera.",
   "start": 79.3918908,
   "end": 81.8355844
  }
 ],
